WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.180
Hello everyone, welcome back to another episode of the Grand Prixquel podcast where we discuss

00:04.180 --> 00:05.840
all things feeder series.

00:05.840 --> 00:10.580
On today's episode, we're going to be doing a recap of basically all the feeder series

00:10.580 --> 00:13.520
races that have happened in the past two weeks.

00:13.520 --> 00:17.720
Your hosts today are myself, Robin, Evan, Nova, and Thia.

00:17.720 --> 00:26.620
Okay, so I guess F2 is up first.

00:26.620 --> 00:31.640
This weekend as part of the whole, you know, Bahrain, Saudi cancellation, we were at Canada

00:31.640 --> 00:33.760
this past week.

00:33.760 --> 00:34.760
Definitely interesting.

00:34.760 --> 00:40.460
Our qualifying had Van Hoepen on pole, I don't know what he was doing, how that happened.

00:40.460 --> 00:42.780
That Trident is, I don't know, but...

00:42.780 --> 00:46.540
Van Hoepen on pole in a Trident is crazy.

00:46.540 --> 00:47.540
Literally.

00:47.540 --> 00:53.660
Yeah, and then alongside that we had Camara second, Dunne third, Tsolov fourth, Stenshorne fifth,

00:54.600 --> 00:57.680
I'm not going to bother going through the whole top ten, it's probably pointless anyway

00:57.680 --> 01:02.760
to go through the whole top ten, but I guess it's almost most of the same usual suspects.

01:02.760 --> 01:09.220
It's important to mention that both Camara and Dunne got penalties.

01:09.220 --> 01:11.100
What was it for? Impeding, I think?

01:11.100 --> 01:16.120
So they both got penalties so they didn't start second and third.

01:16.120 --> 01:20.720
Sprint race, because qualifying- sprint race.

01:20.720 --> 01:28.320
Leon win, Mini second, Stenshorne third, Van Hoepen, Fittipaldi, Beganovic, Camara, Bilinski.

01:28.320 --> 01:33.840
Camara, still, he's just not that good, quite frankly.

01:33.840 --> 01:37.960
I think there were things that happened in the race and I did not write them down clearly,

01:37.960 --> 01:40.520
but he's just not that good.

01:40.520 --> 01:46.560
We had some contact with John Bennett, out of all people, from Stenshorne and Tsolov.

01:47.440 --> 01:53.240
Every single time F2 is mentioned, we milk into the whole Mechachrome bad, car bad, blah

01:53.240 --> 01:54.240
blah blah.

01:54.240 --> 01:58.240
This time it was genuinely like Bennett just got hit and his engine just died.

01:58.240 --> 02:04.720
I think, quite frankly, if we had a starter in the cars, he could have just kept racing.

02:04.720 --> 02:09.160
Of course, Mechachrome decides we don't need to have any starter or any battery or anything

02:09.160 --> 02:15.200
inside the car, so anti-stall is terrible in F2, as anyone who watches knows.

02:15.200 --> 02:19.880
I guess nothing to say other than, you know, unfortunate, but Mechachrome got to sort out

02:19.880 --> 02:20.880
something.

02:20.880 --> 02:24.680
But they weren't, because F2 keeps paying them the big bucks.

02:24.680 --> 02:29.960
And it's also important to note that Alex Dunne had gotten a penalty, again.

02:29.960 --> 02:33.160
Alex Dunne gets a penalty, fork found in kitchen.

02:33.160 --> 02:34.800
He just misses Victor Marlins a little bit.

02:34.800 --> 02:35.800
Yeah.

02:35.800 --> 02:41.160
I feel like he'd be, if he would stop colliding with people, he would be, he'd actually be

02:41.160 --> 02:42.160
better.

02:43.120 --> 02:46.840
Can we talk about Fittipaldi, that being P5?

02:46.840 --> 02:50.200
Yeah, that's a concept and a half.

02:50.200 --> 02:53.480
I honestly, quite frankly, I did not pay attention to him at all.

02:53.480 --> 02:58.760
And when I was writing the notes, I was like, hang on, Fittipaldi P5, okay.

02:58.760 --> 03:00.680
That's certainly something, I suppose.

03:00.680 --> 03:05.120
I don't know how he got the AIX there, considering what happened in the feature race, which we'll

03:05.120 --> 03:07.120
