He has not scored a single point from actually being in a points scoring position.

40:36.180 --> 40:39.180
And I don't know, man.

40:42.180 --> 40:47.180
We had a couple girls from F1 Academy here this weekend as well.

40:47.180 --> 40:50.180
We had Alba, we had Ella, we had Emma.

40:50.180 --> 40:57.180
But none of them really had any results to write home about, unfortunately.

40:58.180 --> 41:01.180
There were a lot of red flags.

41:01.180 --> 41:06.180
We had two races that were red flagged and then restarted.

41:06.180 --> 41:16.180
And I'm actually really happy that after the red flag, they restarted with all the time that they were supposed to run the race.

41:16.180 --> 41:20.180
I don't have the words to describe it.

41:20.180 --> 41:27.180
The 20 minute race, for example, even if they've already done one or two laps and then red flagged it,

41:27.180 --> 41:35.180
when they restarted after the red flag, they restarted the 20 minute countdown, which I'm happy about that.

41:35.180 --> 41:38.180
It gives them more time to race.

41:38.180 --> 41:45.180
But yeah, ended up in an incident where her entire car was covered in dust and sand.

41:45.180 --> 41:51.180
And I don't even know what happened, but her car was like...

41:51.180 --> 41:55.180
It wasn't even that her car was destroyed, it was just covered in dust.

41:57.180 --> 42:03.180
Ella had a DNF at some point and Alba, again, nothing really to write home about.

42:03.180 --> 42:12.180
Chiara ended up on reverse grid pole this weekend, which was very nice.

42:12.180 --> 42:20.180
And unfortunately on both starts-because the reverse grid race was one of the races that got red flagged and restarted-

42:20.180 --> 42:26.180
unfortunately on both starts she lost pole position immediately.

42:26.180 --> 42:33.180
But she ended up on the podium still, so that's always really nice to see.

42:33.180 --> 42:46.180
I think it's been a pretty good weekend for women and motorsports in general, with CHiara on the podium and Abbi winning a race in GB3.

42:46.180 --> 42:52.180
We'll talk a little bit about that in a second, but I just want to finish off with British F4.

42:52.180 --> 43:00.180
George Proudford-Nalder stalled from pole in race 1, which was really unfortunate.

43:00.180 --> 43:05.180
It's always really sad when someone stalls from like the front row.

43:05.180 --> 43:12.180
But he ended up winning race 3, and it was kind of a redemption for him.

43:12.180 --> 43:18.180
One of the races had some really, really close finishes, and I don't remember which one.

43:18.180 --> 43:23.180
And that's the problem with having 3 races in one weekend, is that you don't remember what happened in which race.

43:23.180 --> 43:27.180
But one of the races had a really close finish for the podium.

43:27.180 --> 43:36.180
But then afterwards, both DVL and Ethan Jeff-Hall ended up being penalized from the podium anyways,

43:36.180 --> 43:43.180
which promoted Adam Al-Azhari and Jarrett Clark to the podium instead of them.

43:43.180 --> 43:50.180
DVL was for causing a collision with, I don't remember who, was it Joseph Smith? It might have been Joseph Smith.

43:50.180 --> 43:57.180
And then Ethan Jeff Hall was for an overtaking infringement, which I don't know what that means.

43:57.180 --> 44:01.180
Maybe he overtook someone off track or something. I don't know.

44:01.180 --> 44:04.180
But yeah, I think that's it for British F4.

44:04.180 --> 44:11.180
So in terms of GB3, their race 1 was cancelled because of the weather and everything.

44:11.180 --> 44:19.180
So instead they used the grid from their actual qualifying session for race 2 and cancelled the reverse grid.

44:19.180 --> 44:29.180
So Abbi kept her pole position and also went on to win from pole in race 1.

44:30.180 --> 44:35.180
It was really nice to see Abbi win from pole in a non-reverse grid race.

44:35.180 --> 44:42.180
Because we've seen girls get podiums in reverse grid races, but this was purely on merit.

44:42.180 --> 44:47.180
She qualified on pole, she led every single lap, and she won from pole.

44:47.180 --> 44:51.180
And it was really, really nice to see. And I'm very happy for her.

44:51.180 --> 44:54.180
I don't think we have much else to say about GB3.

44:54.180 --> 44:58.180
I did watch all the races, but they were kind of uneventful, unfortunately.

44:58.180 --> 45:00.180
So yeah, not much to say.

45:00.180 --> 45:10.180
So for championship standings, Nikita Bedrin still leads the championship on 140 points ahead of Maxim Rehm, who is on 113.

45:10.180 --> 45:19.180
Nakamura is currently third, but I think there's a couple of rounds that'll clash with F3 that he won't be able to compete in.

45:19.180 --> 45:26.180
So unfortunately he probably won't keep the P3 until the end of the season, but still some pretty good showings from him.

45:27.180 --> 45:33.180
Abbi is sixth in the championship right now, after her win in race 1.

45:33.180 --> 45:40.180
And yeah, GB3 is not a very big championship. We've had 23 drivers.

45:40.180 --> 45:44.180
So there's not much else to say, I think.

45:46.180 --> 45:49.180
So that's it for today's episode of the Grand Prixquel Podcast.

45:49.180 --> 45:52.180
I hope you guys enjoyed listening.

45:52.180 --> 45:58.180
Make sure to follow us on all our socials, Twitter, Instagram, and TikTok, at Grand Prixquel.

45:58.180 --> 46:03.180
And let us know if you have any comments or anything you want to say about anything we discussed today.

46:03.180 --> 46:12.180
On our next episode, we are going to be doing another review of the upcoming Feeder Series weekend, which has way too many series for me to name.

46:12.180 --> 46:16.180
So make sure to tune in for that next week.

46:16.180 --> 46:18.180
Thank you for listening.


